    "q-351634": {
      "dom_id": "step-q351634",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14253507/assets/d2679e73f59693cc076820af689a63cec573833b9d88a1a00bba81671d39d745.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ bounded between the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=t,\\,y=t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\n$$\n\nand the $x$-axis for $t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The unsigned area bounded by the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=x(t),\\,y=y(t),\\,{t}_{1}\\le t\\le {t}_{2}\n$$\n\nand the $x$-axis is given by the absolute value of the integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}y\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the integral expression\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}y\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that this integral will give us a positive number since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\ge 0$ for all $t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]$ and $t\\ge 0.$\n\nTo solve the above integral, we use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=t & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & ⇒ & v=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-\\frac{t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)}{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}+\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t| \\\\  & =|\\,-\\frac{t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)}{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}+\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t\\,| \\\\  & =|\\,-\\frac{t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)}{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,| \\\\  & =|\\,-\\frac{\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡0}{2}+\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡0)\\,| \\\\  & =|\\,\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,| \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
